stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    state "Recorded, nothing mapped to it" as DRAFT
    state "Registrations being obtained" as PENDING
    state "Filing scope, employments mapped" as ACTIVE
    state "No mapped employment, ledger open" as DORMANT
    state "Retired, history and registers kept" as CLOSED

    [*] --> DRAFT: EST1 establishment recorded with state, sphere and addresses
    DRAFT --> PENDING: EST2 a registration task opens for a scheme the master shows as due
    DRAFT --> ACTIVE: EST3 every registration the recorded obligations need is on file, checked
    PENDING --> ACTIVE: EST4 a registration code recorded as an addition and checked
    ACTIVE --> PENDING: EST5 a new obligation turns on and its registration is not yet held
    ACTIVE --> DORMANT: EST6 last mapped employment ends and no month is open beyond the ledger
    DORMANT --> ACTIVE: EST7 an employment is mapped again
    DORMANT --> CLOSED: EST8 filing ledger shows no open month and closure is checked
    CLOSED --> [*]

    note right of PENDING
        Liabilities compute and show while a
        registration is missing. Payroll is never
        blocked. The member line for the scheme
        is non-fileable until the code is held.
    end note

    note right of DORMANT
        Registers keep their own retention clocks
        from their last entry. Closing never
        shortens a clock and never deletes a row.
    end note

    note right of CLOSED
        Refused while any month on the filing
        ledger is open, while any mapping is
        live, or while a gated change on the
        establishment is waiting for its checker.
    end note
